{"tool_name":"andom","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"andom","home":"http://andom.bioapps.biozentrum.uni-wuerzburg.de/index_new.html","summary":"Web tool that helps to assign structural domains to protein sequences and to classify them according to SCOP.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:36:20Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:17:13.978877Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"collections":["Proteomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:andom","credit":[{"name":"Dominik Schaack & Steffen Schmidt","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.bork.embl.de/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://andom.bioapps.biozentrum.uni-wuerzburg.de/Usage_new.html"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Protein sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2479"},{"term":"Structure classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2996"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Protein structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0474"}]}],"name":"AnDom","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1021/ci010374r","metadata":{"abstract":"The WEB tool \"AnDom\" assigns to a given protein sequence all experimentally determined structural domains contained within it, including multidomain and large proteins. The server uses profile specific matrices from custom generated multiple sequence alignments of all known SCOP domains (SCOP version 1.50). Prediction time is short allowing numerous applications for structural genomics including investigation of complex eucaryotic protein families. The WWW server is at http://www.bork.embl-heidelberg.de/AnDom, and profiles can be downloaded at ftp.bork.embl-heidelberg.de/pub/users/schmidt/AnDom.","authors":[{"name":"Bork P."},{"name":"Dandekar T."},{"name":"Schmidt S."}],"citationCount":14,"date":"2002-03-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Jo